The proof is left as an exercise to the reader. (Hint: show that

\[\|\,\theta_{h}\|_{0,\,\Gamma_{h}}^{2}\leqslant(C/h)\,\|\,\theta_{h}\|_{0,\, \Omega}^{2}\qquad\forall\theta_{h}\in\mathcal{O}_{h}.\]

The next lemma derives an analogue of Corollary A.3.

**Lemma 2.8**.: _If \(\mathcal{T}_{h}\) is a uniformly regular family of triangulations of \(\bar{\Omega},\) there exists a constant \(C>0,\) independent of h, such that:_

(2.55) \[\|\,\theta_{h}\|_{2,\,h}\leqslant(C/h)\,|\theta_{h}|_{1,\,\Omega}\qquad \forall\theta_{h}\in\mathcal{O}_{h}.\]

Proof.: If we apply formula (A.31) with \(r=p=2\) to \(\mathbf{grad}\,\theta_{h}\) in each \(\kappa\) we obtain:

\[|\,\theta_{h}|_{2,\,\kappa}\leqslant(C_{1}/h)\,|\,\theta_{h}|_{1,\,\kappa} \qquad\forall\kappa\in\mathcal{T}_{h}.\]

Thus it remains to establish that

(2.56) \[\|\,S(\partial\theta_{h}/\partial n)\|_{0,\,\Gamma_{h}}^{2}\leqslant(C_{2}/h) \,|\,\theta_{h}|_{1,\,\Omega}^{2}\qquad\forall\theta_{h}\in\mathcal{O}_{h}.\]

Let \(\kappa\) be an arbitrary element of \(\mathcal{T}_{h}.\) In view of (A.9) and (A.2) we get:

\[\int_{\partial\kappa}|\partial\theta_{h}/\partial n|^{2}\,ds \leqslant\int_{\partial\kappa}\,\|\,\mathbf{grad}\,\theta_{h}\|^{ 2}\,ds\] \[\leqslant C_{3}(h_{\kappa}/\rho_{\kappa}^{2})\,\|\,\mathbf{grad} \,\hat{\theta}_{h}\|_{0,\,\partial\kappa}^{2}.\]

But \(\mathbf{grad}\,\hat{\theta}_{h}\) belongs to the finite-dimensional space \(P_{t-1}^{2}\) and therefore

\[\int_{\partial\kappa}|\partial\theta_{h}/\partial n|^{2}\,ds\leqslant C_{4}( \sigma_{\kappa}/\rho_{\kappa})|\,\hat{\theta}_{h}|_{1,\,\kappa}^{2}.\]

Then (A.7), (A.2) and (A.4) give (2.56). 

Of course, it is not possible to extend (2.54) to \(H^{1}(\Omega)\) but we can readily prove the next relation:

**Lemma 2.9**.: _If \(\mathcal{T}_{h}\) is uniformly regular there exists a constant \(C>0,\) independent of h, such that:_

(2.57) \[\|\,\theta\|_{0,\,h}\leqslant C(\|\,\theta\|_{0,\,\Omega}^{2}+h^{2}|\theta|_{ 1,\,\Omega}^{2})^{1/2}\quad\quad\forall\theta\in H^{1}(\Omega).\]

Proof.: Owing to the trace Theorem I.1.5 there exists a constant \(C_{1},\) independent of the geometry of \(\kappa\) such that

\[\|\,\theta\|_{0,\,\kappa^{\prime}}^{2}\leqslant C_{1}\,h_{\kappa}\|\,\hat{ \theta}\|_{1,\,\kappa}^{2}\quad\quad\forall\theta\in H^{1}(\kappa).\]

Then (A.7), (A.2), (A.4) and (A.16) yield:

\[\|\,\theta\|_{0,\,\kappa^{\prime}}^{2}\leqslant C_{2}\,\sigma^{2}[1/(\tau h)\, \|\,\theta\|_{0,\,\kappa}^{2}+h|\theta|_{1,\,\kappa}^{2}],\]

thus proving (2.57). 

